WEBVTT

00:01.880 --> 00:06.150
Mother, I stumbled upon the Black Rose in Salzburg.

00:07.030 --> 00:09.410
He criticized me for losing my brooch.

00:09.780 --> 00:12.580
The mechanical car has also broken down.

00:13.790 --> 00:16.050
What should I do?

00:26.100 --> 00:27.400
NAAJA

00:26.100 --> 00:27.400
Nadja,

00:27.520 --> 00:30.070
With your eyes

00:27.520 --> 00:30.070
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:30.070 --> 00:31.280
Nadja,

00:30.070 --> 00:31.280
NAAJA

00:31.320 --> 00:33.570
What do you see?

00:31.320 --> 00:33.570
Nani ga mieru

00:33.610 --> 00:36.490
Shining in the far distance,

00:33.610 --> 00:36.490
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:36.490 --> 00:38.870
The door to the future,

00:36.490 --> 00:38.870
Mirai no tobira

00:39.780 --> 00:43.250
That's what I'm searching for

00:39.780 --> 00:43.250
Sagashite iru

00:43.250 --> 00:50.460
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.170 --> 00:54.670
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:51.170 --> 00:54.670
Minna egao de aetara

00:54.760 --> 00:58.010
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:54.760 --> 00:58.010
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:58.050 --> 01:01.260
It could be so much more fun

00:58.050 --> 01:01.260
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

01:01.310 --> 01:04.730
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:01.310 --> 01:04.730
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

01:05.100 --> 01:08.400
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.100 --> 01:08.400
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:08.520 --> 01:11.860
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:08.520 --> 01:11.860
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:12.020 --> 01:15.610
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:12.020 --> 01:15.610
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:15.650 --> 01:17.780
I will go waving

01:15.650 --> 01:17.780
Te wo furinagara

01:17.860 --> 01:24.540
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:17.860 --> 01:24.540
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:24.580 --> 01:27.290
But I won't look back

01:24.580 --> 01:27.290
Ushiro mukanai

01:27.620 --> 01:32.590
Until the day my dream comes true

01:27.620 --> 01:32.590
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:32.880 --> 01:36.300
Nadja, Your smile

01:32.880 --> 01:36.300
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:36.380 --> 01:39.720
Nadja, gives me courage

01:36.380 --> 01:39.720
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:39.760 --> 01:42.680
Under the blue sky,

01:39.760 --> 01:42.680
Aoi sora no shita de

01:42.800 --> 01:45.640
I will find the place

01:42.800 --> 01:45.640
Ashita no yukue

01:45.930 --> 01:49.850
where my future lies

01:45.930 --> 01:49.850
Mitsukeru kara

01:55.070 --> 02:00.530
Herman's Mansion

02:13.540 --> 02:15.670
﻿Looks like you've woken up.

02:24.050 --> 02:25.600
﻿Water...

02:27.220 --> 02:32.770
﻿I can see you're defeated by the severe torture, but Master Herman isn't that nice, I'm afraid.

02:37.070 --> 02:37.860
﻿This...

02:38.240 --> 02:40.530
﻿Th-that's..

02:41.030 --> 02:42.240
﻿Please...

02:42.820 --> 02:44.160
﻿water...

02:44.530 --> 02:45.410
﻿B-But...

02:45.450 --> 02:49.330
﻿I won't tell your partner or Herman...

02:51.540 --> 02:52.580
﻿Wait.

02:59.670 --> 03:01.930
﻿Here. Keep it a secret.

03:19.190 --> 03:22.990
﻿I'm afraid I'm not that nice either.

03:33.870 --> 03:38.960
The "Recover the Brooch" Strategy

03:40.590 --> 03:41.420
﻿Nadja...

03:46.300 --> 03:48.510
﻿What!? Why are you--

03:51.020 --> 03:52.020
﻿The brooch...

04:02.740 --> 04:05.200
﻿Is it Rosema-I mean, Nadja?

04:11.870 --> 04:13.160
﻿Y-You...!

04:16.750 --> 04:20.250
﻿I will have the Premingers' brooch.

04:21.670 --> 04:22.210
﻿Stop!

04:27.180 --> 04:28.470
﻿Master Herman!

04:28.510 --> 04:30.510
﻿What on earth were you two idiots doing?!

04:32.220 --> 04:33.270
﻿Sorry...

04:41.360 --> 04:47.320
Salzburg

04:53.330 --> 04:56.460
﻿Nadja. it's no use being frustrated.

04:56.580 --> 05:01.460
﻿The car won't budge until we get that cog we ordered.

05:01.800 --> 05:03.170
﻿That's right.

05:03.170 --> 05:05.510
﻿There's nothing to do except wait and take things easy.

05:05.670 --> 05:10.640
﻿I can't wait and do nothing until the car's fixed, though!

05:10.850 --> 05:12.890
﻿Even if you say so...

05:13.100 --> 05:15.680
﻿There must be something I could do until then!

05:16.100 --> 05:17.770
﻿So anyway, I'm going!

05:17.770 --> 05:18.980
﻿Hey Nadja!

05:19.860 --> 05:21.310
﻿She's gone...

05:25.030 --> 05:27.490
﻿so, I'm out..

05:28.530 --> 05:30.370
﻿But what am I going to do?

05:31.370 --> 05:33.580
﻿I wonder what there is I could do..

05:34.870 --> 05:37.330
﻿What should I do at times like these...?

05:47.420 --> 05:48.510
﻿What is this..

05:49.590 --> 05:51.220
﻿an English map!

06:02.810 --> 06:06.530
﻿That's Salzburg...and this is Vienna..

06:07.610 --> 06:11.450
﻿They're both in the same country but they're so far away.

06:12.200 --> 06:15.490
﻿But if I go here, there must be some clue leading to my mother!

06:16.330 --> 06:18.080
﻿Let's do your best, Nadja

06:18.580 --> 06:19.250
﻿Yeah!

06:30.130 --> 06:31.640
﻿This is it.

06:32.720 --> 06:35.260
﻿The Salzburg Association of Detectives...

06:40.060 --> 06:41.520
﻿Excuse me!

06:42.690 --> 06:43.730
﻿Welcom--

06:44.150 --> 06:45.440
﻿Oh, a child.

06:45.730 --> 06:48.400
﻿There's something I want to ask...

06:48.900 --> 06:51.150
﻿Ask...what?

06:51.610 --> 06:54.450
﻿This is an association of detectives isn't it?

06:54.450 --> 06:55.490
﻿Yes it is.

06:55.660 --> 07:00.160
﻿Then do you know anything about detectives called "Rosso" and "Bianco"?

07:00.160 --> 07:03.000
﻿I've had a terrible time because of them...

07:05.170 --> 07:06.040
﻿I don't know.

07:06.040 --> 07:10.170
﻿Hey, how could you make an assertion when you haven't examined anything?

07:10.470 --> 07:12.800
﻿This is an association of detectives.

07:12.800 --> 07:15.640
﻿but information about out co-workers is top secret.

07:15.640 --> 07:19.390
﻿Even if I knew. I wouldn't tell you.

07:21.890 --> 07:24.520
﻿How dare he treat me like a child!

07:25.310 --> 07:27.150
﻿Then I'll go to the library.

07:38.120 --> 07:39.200
﻿I can't read.

07:40.080 --> 07:42.870
﻿Hey hey, what is the matter?

07:43.040 --> 07:46.960
﻿I'm sorry, but I can't do anything unless you're with me, Abel!

07:52.760 --> 07:54.470
﻿I see.

07:55.140 --> 07:57.600
﻿If it's German, leave it to me.

07:57.850 --> 07:59.890
﻿Abel...thank you

08:00.560 --> 08:02.930
﻿So, what are we going to research?

08:02.930 --> 08:04.440
﻿About the House of Preminger.

08:04.600 --> 08:09.770
﻿Since Vienna's in the same country as Austria, I thought there'd be something useful here...

08:09.770 --> 08:13.650
﻿Okay. Then let's search for some books over there first.

08:45.270 --> 08:46.850
﻿Nadja. Look at this.

08:49.440 --> 08:51.860
﻿It's a genealogy of the House of Preminger.

08:53.940 --> 08:54.860
﻿This is enormous.

08:55.200 --> 08:57.660
﻿Looks like it competes with the other Austrian families for first place.

08:58.200 --> 09:01.080
﻿Is there a woman's name in here somewhere?

09:01.080 --> 09:08.170
﻿If it's around your mother's age... Eva, Maria, Colette. These three are women.

09:08.170 --> 09:11.630
﻿Three women... And one of them is...

09:17.630 --> 09:20.970
﻿What are you going to do from now on? I'll be going back to the troupe.

09:22.760 --> 09:23.770
﻿The washing!

09:23.770 --> 09:24.470
﻿What?

09:25.100 --> 09:28.190
﻿I need to do the washing It was my turn this time.

09:32.980 --> 09:35.990
I﻿'m sorry! I'll do the rest!

09:37.110 --> 09:38.530
﻿What were you doing until now?

09:38.950 --> 09:39.950
﻿I'm really sorry.

09:39.950 --> 09:42.410
﻿I thought I could find out something about my mother...

09:43.410 --> 09:44.990
﻿Well, okay then...

09:45.700 --> 09:47.870
﻿I'm not that impressed with the slackness, though.

09:51.960 --> 09:52.630
﻿Hey.

09:52.960 --> 09:54.590
﻿Harvey!

09:55.340 --> 09:58.380
﻿What?! Your brooch has been stolen?!

09:58.720 --> 10:00.220
﻿Damn those thieves...

10:00.220 --> 10:03.600
﻿But if I go to Vienna, apparently I can get to know more about my mother.

10:03.560 --> 10:07.480
It's not the time to be happy. Why don't you try and get it back?

10:08.230 --> 10:09.810
﻿There's nothing I can do about it...

10:09.810 --> 10:14.480
﻿I don't know where the two are, and it was stolen in Egypt so...

10:15.110 --> 10:16.400
﻿Are you going to give up then?

10:16.940 --> 10:18.900
﻿I didn't give up because I wanted to!

10:19.030 --> 10:21.820
﻿Don't be mad. There's still a way.

10:22.070 --> 10:22.950
A ﻿way?

10:22.950 --> 10:25.910
﻿Have you forgotten that I'm a journalist?

10:26.200 --> 10:29.000
﻿We'll get that brooch back using pen!

10:29.000 --> 10:30.370
﻿What do you mean?

10:30.370 --> 10:31.960
﻿Make it a newspaper article.

10:32.130 --> 10:35.670
﻿I'll write an article about you and put it on the papers.

10:35.670 --> 10:36.750
﻿Then I want to help.

10:36.750 --> 10:37.590
﻿Huh?

10:37.590 --> 10:39.920
﻿Please... let me help.

10:44.600 --> 10:45.970
﻿Okay then.

10:50.350 --> 10:51.640
﻿What is she doing?

10:51.640 --> 10:54.060
﻿Nadja's drawing a portrait.

10:54.060 --> 10:55.440
﻿Finished!

10:56.480 --> 10:57.280
﻿Does it look like them?

10:58.820 --> 11:01.860
﻿Actually... are they supposed to be human?

11:03.360 --> 11:03.990
﻿And?

11:04.570 --> 11:09.120
﻿I got it back once... but when we got out of the Pyramid they stole it again...

11:10.000 --> 11:14.130
﻿Well then, let's ask the other members of the troupe just in case.

11:14.460 --> 11:18.300
﻿Uh um, l-my name is err K-K-Kennosuke.

11:18.300 --> 11:21.090
﻿Just because it's an interview it doesn't mean you have to be that formal...

11:21.090 --> 11:27.140
﻿"Oh no we're done for!!!" Just when everyone thought that,

11:27.850 --> 11:30.310
﻿the one and only Treasure Hunter-me-came to save the day!

11:30.310 --> 11:32.060
﻿Uhm... it’s not that...

11:35.690 --> 11:38.150
﻿The truth is, Chocolat is white.

11:39.900 --> 11:41.280
﻿Ah...will you go away...?

11:41.280 --> 11:42.780
﻿Whaaat?!

11:43.030 --> 11:44.530
﻿Next please!

11:44.530 --> 11:46.030
﻿What do you mean by 'next'?

11:46.530 --> 11:46.990
Oh,

11:49.910 --> 11:51.370
﻿come on...

11:52.620 --> 11:55.750
﻿Phew... done at last..

11:55.830 --> 11:58.130
﻿What's next? What should I do next?

11:58.340 --> 12:02.510
﻿Say... then let's have you write it too.

12:04.180 --> 12:07.390
﻿Write down all your confessions.

12:09.220 --> 12:10.520
﻿Me?

12:26.280 --> 12:28.240
﻿Herman who stole the brooch..

12:28.910 --> 12:29.740
﻿and...

12:29.950 --> 12:32.040
﻿...that girl who was being called "Nadja"...

12:32.950 --> 12:36.080
﻿What on earth is happening in the House of Preminger...?!

13:08.070 --> 13:11.740
﻿Please... give me back my brooch.

13:12.330 --> 13:16.830
﻿That brooch is an important connection between my yet-seen mother and I.

13:17.460 --> 13:20.040
﻿If I get it back...I won't blame you for what you've done.

13:20.790 --> 13:21.630
﻿So please...!

13:24.010 --> 13:28.720
﻿From Nadja Applefield in Salzburg, Austria.

13:29.300 --> 13:30.300
﻿I see.

13:31.050 --> 13:32.260
﻿How is it?

13:32.510 --> 13:34.520
﻿Okay. It's good.

13:35.350 --> 13:36.600
﻿Phew... good...

13:37.230 --> 13:40.060
﻿All that's left now is for me to turn it into an article...

13:40.060 --> 13:41.150
﻿Thank you!

13:41.610 --> 13:43.570
﻿Leave it to me, see ya.

13:59.250 --> 14:04.210
﻿The girl related to Duke Preminger had her brooch stolen.

14:05.510 --> 14:11.680
﻿Nadja Applefield, 13 years old, from the Applefield Orphanage. England.

14:11.680 --> 14:13.050
﻿had her brooch stolen in Egypt...

14:13.050 --> 14:18.020
﻿by two thugs-self-proclaimed detectives named "Rosso" and "Bianco".

14:18.600 --> 14:22.480
﻿The brooch was Hers since the day she was born,

14:22.480 --> 14:25.190
﻿and it is the only key to finding her blood relation.

14:25.900 --> 14:30.780
﻿From the coat of arms on the ring, she is said to be related to Duke Preminger.

14:31.160 --> 14:40.000
﻿Can the act of two fully grown adults stealing property from a 13 year old girl be forgiven?

14:40.830 --> 14:48.340
﻿Readers who have information on "Rosso" and "Bianco", please contact the police or us.

14:51.220 --> 14:55.100
﻿Good. It's in time for the deadline.

14:55.510 --> 14:59.930
﻿Hey, can someone telegraph this to the Vienna Newspaper and the head office?

15:05.400 --> 15:07.730
﻿Hm... This has gotten quite troublesome...

15:07.730 --> 15:10.150
﻿The Black Rose stealing the brooch was unexpected...

15:10.150 --> 15:12.740
﻿What am I going to say to my father...?

15:12.740 --> 15:15.490
﻿Isn't it better if you told him the truth?

15:15.780 --> 15:18.080
﻿What do you mean by telling him the truth?

15:18.410 --> 15:20.750
﻿That The Black Rose stole the brooch...

15:20.910 --> 15:24.130
﻿How foolish! As if I could say that...

15:26.130 --> 15:28.840
﻿Excuse me, you're Mr. Herman, right?

15:28.840 --> 15:30.050
﻿Can I have a word?

15:30.760 --> 15:33.630
﻿I'm from the Montmartre Journal.

15:33.630 --> 15:37.640
﻿Is it true that the Premingers’ brooch had been stolen?

15:37.970 --> 15:39.180
﻿How do you--

15:39.180 --> 15:40.140
﻿"How"?

15:40.140 --> 15:42.270
﻿Then it's true, yes?

15:42.730 --> 15:45.650
﻿Er...no, actually--

15:45.650 --> 15:46.560
﻿It's true.

15:49.570 --> 15:54.320
﻿My precious brooch was stolen by The Black Rose!

15:54.320 --> 15:55.740
﻿The Black Rose?!

15:55.740 --> 15:59.290
﻿But our coverage says that "Rosso" and "Bianco"-

15:59.290 --> 16:02.120
﻿That must be some mistake.

16:02.120 --> 16:04.920
﻿So then, you're the owner of the brooch--

16:05.210 --> 16:08.460
﻿Yes. I am Nadja.

16:09.710 --> 16:11.800
﻿Nadja Applefield.

16:14.630 --> 16:19.470
﻿Please. That brooch is a special bond between my mother and me.

16:19.470 --> 16:22.640
﻿Please get me back my brooch with the help of your pen!

16:26.230 --> 16:27.690
﻿This girl...

16:28.560 --> 16:30.610
﻿This is going to be a scoop!

16:55.510 --> 16:56.470
﻿Mother...

17:20.910 --> 17:25.330
﻿Really... sneaking into a lady's bedroom at night without permission... How rude.

17:25.330 --> 17:29.000
﻿Sorry. There was no other way.

17:30.880 --> 17:31.540
﻿Nadja.

17:46.810 --> 17:47.690
﻿Here.

17:53.400 --> 17:54.820
﻿My brooch!

17:54.820 --> 17:56.820
﻿You got it back for me?

17:58.820 --> 18:01.320
﻿Thank you... so much..

18:02.030 --> 18:04.040
﻿But... how?

18:04.040 --> 18:08.790
﻿Where was it? You didn't... steal for me, did you...?

18:16.880 --> 18:18.920
﻿I can't accept stolen property.

18:21.640 --> 18:23.850
﻿This isn't stolen property.

18:24.680 --> 18:27.020
﻿I just got back what was stolen.

18:29.690 --> 18:30.730
﻿Keith...

18:37.320 --> 18:42.320
﻿Now... you must never part with the brooch again.

18:45.080 --> 18:45.950
﻿Got it?

18:46.990 --> 18:48.120
﻿Keith...

18:49.870 --> 18:50.920
﻿Thank you.

18:51.870 --> 18:57.380
﻿And one more thing. If you meet a man called "Herman", be careful.

18:59.170 --> 19:00.630
﻿"Herman"?

19:06.720 --> 19:07.850
﻿Keith...

19:11.020 --> 19:13.770
﻿Why did I accept it...

19:14.270 --> 19:16.520
﻿even though I thought that burglary was wrong...?

19:17.690 --> 19:18.690
﻿Keith...

19:36.170 --> 19:38.630
﻿Seems like I overdid things a bit...

19:39.960 --> 19:41.340
﻿It's alright...

19:41.760 --> 19:44.430
﻿If a take a little rest..

20:05.320 --> 20:07.030
﻿The brooch!

20:12.460 --> 20:13.790
You g﻿ot it back?

20:13.790 --> 20:15.750
﻿How did you get it back?

20:15.750 --> 20:18.460
﻿I'm sorry. I can't say.

20:18.670 --> 20:20.630
﻿What?! "Can’t say"?

20:21.710 --> 20:24.550
﻿Well, life is full of various happenings, isn't it?

20:24.550 --> 20:25.510
﻿Granny...

20:25.510 --> 20:27.800
﻿Let's trust Nadja.

20:27.800 --> 20:28.760
﻿Everyone...

20:31.310 --> 20:35.810
﻿Everyone has a thing or two that they can't talk about to others.

20:36.650 --> 20:42.280
﻿Now that Nadja's brooch is back, let's depart for Vienna!

20:42.360 --> 20:47.450
﻿We have to tell Harvey about the brooch and have the article canceled...

20:47.620 --> 20:52.040
﻿But it was really stolen anyway... so it'll be alright, won't it?

20:52.040 --> 20:56.830
﻿And if things go well, those ruffians may be caught.

20:57.080 --> 20:58.540
﻿Yeah, but...

20:59.040 --> 21:03.300
﻿Anyway, going to Vienna is first priority, for Nadja also.

21:03.340 --> 21:04.800
﻿Let's go, everyone!

21:04.840 --> 21:05.930
﻿Yeah!

21:07.550 --> 21:09.300
﻿Thank you... everyone...

21:18.900 --> 21:23.110
﻿Now... where might that article about Nadja be...

21:26.610 --> 21:32.240
﻿Wh-What is this article?! It's completely different than the one I wrote!

21:32.910 --> 21:38.710
﻿The Black Rose steals a brooch from the separated grandchild of Duke Preminger.

21:39.580 --> 21:41.960
﻿Quite well done, it is.

21:53.930 --> 22:01.810
Little did Nadja know that The Black Rose and Harvey's actions of benevolence

22:02.230 --> 22:05.650
had been turned into new obstacles for them to overcome...

22:13.700 --> 22:16.950
Paris is sunnier than London

22:13.700 --> 22:16.950
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:17.080 --> 22:20.170
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:17.080 --> 22:20.170
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:20.580 --> 22:26.760
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:20.580 --> 22:26.760
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:27.720 --> 22:28.970
Indeed

22:27.720 --> 22:28.970
Kitto

22:31.720 --> 22:34.140
It's not use worrying about it

22:31.720 --> 22:34.140
Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:34.720 --> 22:37.850
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:34.720 --> 22:37.850
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:38.140 --> 22:42.860
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:38.140 --> 22:42.860
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:42.940 --> 22:44.320
To be, to be

22:42.940 --> 22:44.320
Naru naru

22:44.650 --> 22:49.650
The tree fog won

22:44.650 --> 22:49.650
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:50.110 --> 22:54.030
The world frog-jumping contest

22:50.110 --> 22:54.030
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:57.240 --> 23:03.420
Under the kitten's paw

22:57.240 --> 23:03.420
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:03.830 --> 23:10.010
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:03.830 --> 23:10.010
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:12.840 --> 23:16.180
Paris is sunnier than London

23:12.840 --> 23:16.180
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:16.260 --> 23:19.220
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

23:16.260 --> 23:19.220
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:19.730 --> 23:26.110
It's not the time to hang around

23:19.730 --> 23:26.110
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:26.980 --> 23:31.490
Indeed, indeed

23:26.980 --> 23:31.490
Kitto kitto

23:39.830 --> 23:41.290
Tomorrow's Nadja

23:43.080 --> 23:45.580
﻿There is another Nadja that I don't know...

23:46.040 --> 23:50.550
Who are you? What are you going to do by taking my place?

23:50.550 --> 23:53.050
﻿I'm going to find out who you are...

23:54.090 --> 23:55.010
﻿You're—

23:55.800 --> 23:57.760
Why? Why is it?

23:58.510 --> 23:59.470
﻿St— Stop it!!

23:59.600 --> 24:01.930
what are you doing to my mother's dress?!

24:02.170 --> 24:03.200
Tomorrow's Nadja.

24:03.310 --> 24:05.760
Rosemary -- The Scheme Behind the Smile

24:05.390 --> 24:07.400
﻿Now, the door of destiny opens.
